====================================================================================================
[1] CHECK 3b: PRE-ACCELERATION -- symmetric vs retarded on a quiet->loud worldline (a0=1 units)
====================================================================================================
    quiet x = 0.1, loud x = 1.0: mu_quiet = 0.2711, mu_loud = 0.6321
    SYMMETRIC form assigns the pre-onset epoch mu_sym = 0.5019 -> pre-response at 64% of the full quiet->loud shift, BEFORE the force changes.
    (acausality is O(1) -- the modulus-Fourier functional reads the future at full strength;
     it decays only as the loud epoch's share of the window -> no exponential protection.)
    RETARDED estimator pre-onset deviation: max |A_ret - A_quiet|/A_quiet = 1.03e-02 (window ripple only, ~1/(2 pi N_cyc) = 1.99e-02; ZERO future response)  PASS
    transient-MOND-boost fingerprint: immediately post-step the stale window gives response enhancement mu_loud/mu_ret = 2.320 (-> 1 as the window fills; half-life 1.2 cycles = 0.14 N_cyc -- mu's steep rise at small A front-loads the recovery; full refill ~ N_cyc)
    ALD comparison: the M22 law is SECOND order plus memory -- no third derivative ever appears, so
    the ALD runaway/pre-acceleration disease (and its order-reduction cure) has no analog here; the
    analog risk is multivaluedness of the implicit mu-solve, closed in [2] by monotone x*mu(x).

